{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Natural World", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Animal Exploitation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Identify and describe events in the news in a range of social and work contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about animal exploitation.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "circus ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a traveling company of acrobats, trained animals, and clowns that gives performances, typically in a large tent.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We often see animals performing in circuses.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the public eye", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in front of people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When the circus animals are out of the public eye, they are sometimes mistreated.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "misery ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "great sadness or unhappiness ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They often face a life of misery and pain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cage", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a small enclosure that you cannot escape from ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Animals are often kept in cages that are too small for them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "claw", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a curved pointed nail on each digit of the foot in birds, lizards, and some mammals like lions and tigers. ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The trainers remove their claws.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "muzzle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a device placed around the mouth of an animal to keep them quiet and to prevent biting ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Trainers put muzzles on their mouths.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tranquilizing", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having a calming or sedative effect", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are sometimes given tranquilizing drugs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bullfight", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a public show, particularly in Spain, Portugal, and Latin America, at which a bull is baited and then usually killed for entertainment", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In some countries where bullfights are popular, people get excited when the bulls die a painful death.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tear", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to rip", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: In other countries, dogs are trained to tear each other apart.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rooster", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a male chicken", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sharp metal points are put on roosters to kill each other in what people call \"cockfights.\"", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for Clarification and Emphasizing a Point", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You ask for clarification when you want more details on what the other person is talking about. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can emphasize a point by asking rhetorical questions. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You ask for clarification when it is not clear what the other person is referring to. You ask the other person to be more specific by giving you more information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use a question at the beginning of a statement or question to ask for clarification like: <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it sounds a bit too intense?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> is a question that is included inside another one.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Direct question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> What are you going to do after dinner?</span><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question:</span> <span class=\"italic\"> Do you know what you're going to do after dinner?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below for an explanation on how to make embedded questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can also use <span class=\"strong\">rhetorical questions</span> to emphasize a point. You use them to make a point rather than to invite an answer from the listener. Rhetorical questions are questions that don't need to be answered.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">What are you going to do?</span> (when there is nothing to be done)<br/><span class=\"italic\">How about that?</span> (when you want to make a point) <br/><span class=\"italic\">Are you kidding me?</span> (when you are upset or surprised)<br/><span class=\"italic\">How should I know?</span> (when you don't know the answer)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Main Question</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Embedded Question</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you know \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"where they train the animals?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Do you remember\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"when we saw the dancing monkeys?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Can you tell me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"who the best trainer is?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Could you tell me \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"what the names of the animals are?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Can you tell me how animals in entertainment are really feeling?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Do you know what we can do about this?  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Is there anything that can be done?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Be careful! If the embedded question includes an auxiliary verb or the verb <span class=\"italic\">to be</span>, you must reverse the positions of the subject and the auxiliary verb. <br><br> Examples: <br> <span class=\"strong\">Direct question:</span> <span class=\"strong\">Can you</span> help me? <br> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question:</span> I wonder if <span class=\"strong\">you can</span> help me. <br> <span class=\"strong\">Direct question:</span><span class=\"strong\"> Is she</span> an animal trainer?  <br> <span class=\"strong\">Embedded question:</span> Do you know if <span class=\"strong\">she is</span> an animal trainer?", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Showing That You Understand Someone's Feelings", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> followed by an adjective when you want to empathize with someone. When you empathize with someone, you show them that you understand their feelings.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Here is the structure to follow:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + must + verb + adjective", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You must feel depressed. <br/>You must be excited.<br/> They must be shocked!<br/> It must be terrifying to do that!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use either <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span> adjectives or <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't forget to include the verb before the adjective.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Paul</span>: I've stayed up all night.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: You must be tired.</span>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Tania</span>: It must be fascinating living in Europe.<br/><span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: Yeah, it is!", "type": "example"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le12ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, discuss this statement: All animal performances should be illegal. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do you agree or disagree? Explain your opinion to your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to show empathy and ask embedded questions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask follow-up questions to keep the conversation going.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I discuss a controversial topic with my partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I communicate empathy.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for clarification and emphasize my point.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": []